{"kind":"report","text":"Preliminary static I1 review completed: repairs at exact 10d3f1bf71f25a7732a7e3c5af5da565c57333b7 from reviewed 479987f6cb34d6aaf0d23d309c6d059f536f9b48, then composition/dispatch at d9bcfb33d019bdf2397ebc75739fa1705eb0862a. This is not final ordinary I1 approval.\n\nP2 — The timed-entry estimator loses party-list multiplicity. validate.ts:782 substitutes scalar member for every party slot; actual slot typing at 253 gives a list its list(member,max), assignable:99 and copy:467 permit copying it to a compatible ref, and effects.ts:94 copies the entire slot. Legal witness: untimed genesis root; one non-hold job, waiting live and done final; mutable people party list max32; mutable saved ref to list(member,max32); required immutable until time set at opening; ordinary guarded acts add one member each; timed finish copies people into saved and sets done, with no attention or sends. At entryBytes4096, the estimator gives 2805 (768+8+128+7+1760+128+6), but 32 short handles @m00–@m31 with ordinary membership references take 5025 bytes for the copied list alone. Root and lifecycle audit independently serialized only synthetic plain JSON data for that arithmetic, using scope/incarnation identifier lengths verified against static encoding source; no project/evaluator was invoked. A correctly authorized ordinary addition contains only one member in its field and one in its effect and can fit. Thus a definition accepted under these same bounds can acquire a permanently unwriteable timed transition. The new Unfit catch returns unavailable/reschedules and keeps the item due; it does not make that admitted transition fit. Preserve the party list's real type and maximum in the estimate, preferably reuse normalized slot typing. Validator/effects/values are byte-identical at d9, so this persists there. This refines the existing timed-size repair and essential-settlement ownership, rather than commissioning another timer model.\n\nP2 — Enforce the HTTP body limit in bytes while consuming it. d9 worker.ts:113–114 first buffers all of request.text(), then compares UTF-16 string.length with BODY_BYTES. Delta111 (:434) claims at most1MiB. A valid founding body with an ignored top-level padding string of400000 CJK characters has over1MiB of UTF-8 bytes, under1MiB of code units, and reaches the underlying operation. Even an ASCII oversized stream has already been fully buffered before refusal. Count raw body bytes with a bounded reader and stop/cancel after the limit before parsing or invoking RPC, preserving stable400 behavior. This independently confirms planner5ae48862's existing source observation; no live request was sent and no duplicate broad route project is proposed.\n\nP2 — Refuse malformed path escaping instead of throwing. d9 worker.ts:125 maps decodeURIComponent over the path before a catch. GET /v1/scopes/% raises URIError before a Response is produced. Catch invalid percent/UTF-8 escaping at the route boundary and return a stable malformed-request response. Static source witness only. Nonarray grants do not establish another defect: core.ts:225 converts them to an empty presentation, and malformed settlement signatures fail the guarded signature check at264 and bytes/domains.ts:36–41.\n\nConfirmed repairs and useful behavior: the original oversized attention reason is rejected by the new estimate. The temporary memberBytes256 proposal is explicitly unadopted; field, party and attribution paths enforce it. Accepted actor/key lookup now skips foreign prefetch, so the old lost-dependency receipt/mismatch cases are repaired while the disclosed drain, busy and clock limits remain. L8 parser RangeError now becomes source_complexity rather than an engine fault; L9 forbids binding the pinned engine table plus now/millis, with ordinary data variables preserved. The table was independently compared with static pinned JSONata2.2.2 source. The bracket precheck does not recognize comments, so comment punctuation can overcount or hide lexical nesting; RangeError still becomes a refusal. This is a lower-severity approximation/compatibility limit, not a newly established security bypass or measured parser CPU bound.\n\nComposition: independent reads found no additional material source-authentication or durable-attempt-order defect. Receiver checks source bytes/hash, send ordinal/message/address/incarnation and result origin before recording. The sender writes an unanswered attempt and sets its retry alarm before transport; held genesis sends remain undispatched until confirmation. Tests meaningfully cover provisional child/confirmation, distinct identical-message creations, exact repeats, relationship order, diagnosis, forged source and restart, but their execution/timing remains producer-attributed and their authority/definition/read ports are test wiring. Production authority/readers refuse and the missing child declaration supply is disclosed as step5 work.\n\nExisting obligations stay open: cc570904, promised by a1bd8c18, owns consistent checkpoint policy and the result-clause timer-rearming closure. All114 actual delta rows require current R1/R3/R4 dispositions. Restored-history retransmission, acknowledged requests without a result, unbounded attempt logs and oversized diagnosis, operator conflict/delivery-unavailable recovery, child definitions, authority/client/independent replay, source/component removal and comparable cost evidence remain owed. deliveryBatch limits one query, not an entire dispatch pass; persistent slow traffic can keep a pass running. That work/latency boundary is not claimed to be a newly established contract violation. Production/provider/browser/device acceptance and whole-workflow10x savings are not certified.\n\nArchitecture: one fold and judge remain the authority, with preparation outside synchronous commits and trusted namespace ports for transport. Security: the useful engine-name and source-authentication repairs stand; the body-byte and malformed-path boundaries need the two small corrections above. Simplification: fix normalized party typing and the existing route parser, use compact witnesses in existing fixtures, and preserve the complete scope instead of adding another judge, quota system or heavy suite.\n\nCoverage and provenance: root freshly read all36292 characters of the complete12-path479→10 unified-5 diff, relevant legal slot/effect/timer grammar, and independently checked the plain-data byte arithmetic. Lifecycle audit covered complete current relevant content by prior full reads plus every changed byte, with fresh effects/values/evaluator/profile/answers reading. Evaluator audit freshly read all five rule files, rule test and needed preparation/definition contexts. For10→d9, the bounded-read audit read every changed byte of all23 paths and complete current production files, reads, three composition/net/route tests, test Worker, README and configurations; evaluator audit read the entire current441-line/67343-byte delta note with all114 rows. Root read complete current core, object, delivery, outbox, namespace, worker, ports, store, README, composition/route tests, every new delta96–114 and amended94. Root did not read every byte of the combined131519-character dispatch diff. The exact d9 direct parent is c0b9818dd7676548ff8098127dc01cdc628ae030, not10d3;10d3 is the requested aggregate comparison base. Static file identities/size/hash ledgers are retained in this review session. Current delta-note SHA2563a29d1d3d471bd37dab560d9e7df10e38da47b472af223084b94ace381fdec76; worker e98ea8cd82b58e0d10744fef0efa02283e51e5095fdad16338af0146375d50f0; validator at10 a42cb0718a2b031d1618bdb4258c8ece3077da20ff99bb7f4c99bd7cb7a1b65b.\n\nNo tests, builds, installs, project or private diagnostics, repository code/evaluator probes, source edits or external effects were executed. Preserve the final ordinary whole-I1 route and full functional scope.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true"}}